    "Use full saved scene states at t=0.2039607747661155 and t=0.20833333333333334; no toy geometry.",
    "Warm caches; re-cut/reset the exact frozen input outside timing; replay a complete physical step without committing it.",
    "Compare ordinary wall timing to synchronized nested stage timing; collect a separate CPU/CUDA profiler trace.",
    "Alternate controls on the same state, same precision, same quadrature, same step and tolerances. Eight repetitions for timing; four further repetitions with per-physical-field difference checks."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Late-state ordinary median step = about 373 ms; surface boundary solve accounts for about 304 ms (~82%).",
    "Two production geometric re-cuts total about 26 ms (~7%); contact quadrature construction adds about 13 ms.",
    "The expensive operation is per-quadrature-point B^T diag(d) B implemented by a generic batched matrix product for B=[I,n]. Late state has 138128 points and 7 boundary iterations, with 3 boundary solves per physical step.",
    "The GPU trace maps the large cost to FP64 CUTLASS kernels for batches of 4x3 times 3x4 matrices. The ordinary global geometry and plastic return are not the main cost.",
    "The group-selection wave-step probe computes a full RHS, then the driver recomputes that RHS at the identical state. With no merge, this is one redundant RHS out of three.",
    "CPU synchronization time largely includes waiting for GPU work; it must not be added to GPU kernel time or interpreted as pure host synchronization overhead.",
    "Replacing generic matrix products by the exact B=[I,n] component formula in a temporary diagnostic control is much faster with roundoff-scale single-step differences."
  ],
